The simulations support the untruncated distance correction under independent coefficient-vector sampling. Clipping negative values to zero introduces bias, so “the quantity under the square root” needs to be distinguished from the untruncated estimate. I also confirmed that adding an unlabelled specimen can change automatic H, and that loaded group labels retain spaces, which can make PCA groups differ from the proposed collections.

